New buildStartState():
- users: INTERNAL (seed.ts:49-65, 15 people) plus the contacts of ONE supplier (keep s1 Solvaro Oleochemicals S.A., seed.ts:68, with Elena Márquez and Ravi Menon);
- suppliers: [s1];
- templates: v1 published, v2 draft (seed.ts:392-395);
- activeRuleSet: RS-2026.1;
- ownership and reminders as today;
- cases: [] and mails: [];
- personaId: 'rmm'.
StoreProvider loads this when localStorage is empty, and Reset returns to it.

Bump SCHEMA to 7 so a browser that has old seeded data falls back to the empty start. In the morning, open http://localhost:5310 in a fresh profile or after clearing the key, and verify:
- 0 cases;
- 1 supplier;
- every persona switchable;
- every inbox empty;
- every list shows its empty state.

Cancellation:
- also marks every open track as ended and writes a 'Task ended' entry per track;
- sends a neutral 'request withdrawn' mail to the contacts and a mail to every assignee with an open task.
Reactivation:
- refused at action level after 365 days;
- asks for an optional reason;
- mails the contacts and the assignees.

State mails[] with id, to, caseId, opId, event, subject, body, at and read. Route /inbox (internal) and /portal/inbox (supplier); list plus reading pane; an unread badge in the shells; a deep link to the case or the portal request.
Open-point recipients (R-1, one generic template 'Someone has written on <case> · <reference>'):
- raise, edit, close (accept, not accepted, withdrawn) and return go to every invited contact of the case;
- an answer goes to the raiser and the responsible person.
Other events:
- invitation (PROC-004);
- review tasks and informed mails (PROC-017);
- added sections (CFG-008);
- Part 2 changes (PROC-031);
- the single release request (PROC-040);
- final document to RMM (R2-01);
- change attempt (PROC-043);
- cancel and reactivate (PROC-049);
- reminders and escalation (REM-01).
Supplier mails carry no question text or internal content, only the material, the case ID, the reference and the link.

Vitest, starting from buildStartState. Cover:
- addSupplier and addContact validations (DUNS, unique e-mail, at least one contact);
- edit and close of an open point (thread entries, status, blocking, mails);
- the mail recipients for each R-1 event;
- the single release mail;
- the final-document snapshot content and immutability;
- freeze guards and the logged attempt;
- cancellation ends the tracks; the reactivation window;
- every finding blocks;
- reminders under the demo clock;
- ownership pinned per case.
Existing tests move to buildDemoSeed.
